<title>TURKEY: Turkish Aksa Q1 profits rise 51.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Turkish Aksa Q1 profits rise 51.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   565.77 vs     708.09</p>
<p>    Net profit		  1,888.71 vs   1,244.11</p>
<p>    Net sales		  10,392.87 vs   5,314.38</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  2,613.47 vs   1,451.63</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  957.95 vs     727.12</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 495.78 vs     224.83</p>
<p>    Interest paid		 139.68 vs	71.54</p>
<p>    Total debts		10,255.94 vs   6,185.07</p>
<p>    Equity		     12,872.51 vs   7,333.68</p>
<p>    Capital		     3,338.30 vs   1,757.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Acrylic-based tow and fibre producer Aksa Akrilik Kimya Sanayi A.S. is owned largely by Akkok textile group.</p>
<p>It decided to raise its capital to 5,675.1 billion lira by issuing 0.5 rights and 0.2 bonus for one existing share. It will also start distributing a 850 lira dividend per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from 1996 profits on May 30.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
